From: RocksDB z/OS Port <zopen@rocksdb>
Date: 2025-01-01
Subject: [PATCH 5a/9] z/OS: add new file port/zos_compat.h

z/OS lacks several Linux/glibc-specific identifiers:
  - O_DIRECT / O_DIRECTORY : not defined; map to 0 (safe no-op)
  - fread_unlocked          : glibc extension; map to standard fread
  - major() / minor()       : no <sys/sysmacros.h> on z/OS; stub to 0
    so the same-device check in GetFreeSpace always passes (conservative)

ZOS_TAG_FD_BINARY(fd) tags an open fd as binary (CCSID 65535) so the
z/OS kernel never auto-converts pread/pwrite bytes. It calls
__chgfdccsid(fd, 65535) which is present as a T (code) symbol in
libzoslib.a (confirmed via nm). The extern "C" declaration prevents
C++ name-mangling. libzoslib.a is already on every tool link line.

fcntl(F_SETTAG) does not work on this z/OS system (returns EINVAL).
__chgfdccsid in libzoslib.a is the correct working implementation.

diff --git a/port/zos_compat.h b/port/zos_compat.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/port/zos_compat.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+// Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
+// This source code is licensed under both the GPLv2 (found in the
+// COPYING file in the root directory) and Apache 2.0 License
+// (found in the LICENSE.Apache file in the root directory).
+//
+// z/OS compatibility shims for identifiers absent from z/OS system headers.
+// Include early in files that use Linux/glibc-specific extensions.
+#pragma once
+#if defined(__MVS__)
+#  ifndef O_DIRECT
+#    define O_DIRECT   0
+#  endif
+#  ifndef O_DIRECTORY
+#    define O_DIRECTORY 0
+#  endif
+#  ifndef fread_unlocked
+#    define fread_unlocked fread
+#  endif
+#  ifndef major
+#    define major(dev) (0)
+#    define minor(dev) (0)
+#  endif
+// z/OS file-tag: tag an open fd as ISO-8859-1/ASCII (CCSID 819) so the
+// z/OS kernel treats bytes as ASCII without EBCDIC conversion.
+// CCSID 819 = ISO-8859-1 = ASCII: correct for RocksDB data files written
+// by an ASCII-mode process (-fzos-le-char-mode=ascii). CCSID 65535 (raw
+// binary) prevents all display tools from reading the files correctly.
+// __chgfdccsid is a T-symbol in libzoslib.a (confirmed via nm).
+// extern "C" prevents C++ name-mangling; libzoslib.a is on every link.
+extern "C" int __chgfdccsid(int fd, unsigned short ccsid);
+#  ifndef ZOS_TAG_FD_BINARY
+#    define ZOS_TAG_FD_BINARY(fd) \
+         do { if ((fd) >= 0) (void)__chgfdccsid((fd), 819U); } while (0)
+#  endif
+#else
+#  define ZOS_TAG_FD_BINARY(fd) ((void)(fd))
+#endif

